  "notes": [
    "Built from the 2013 video method and the published Sanjeev Kapoor ingredient list. Where they differ, the published quantities are used; the video lists 3 tbsp lemon juice, while the published recipe lists 3 tsp (15 mL).",
    "Use food-safe charcoal. Heat it until fully glowing, set it in a small steel bowl inside the gravy, and add the butter to the bowl. Do not let ash fall into the pan.",
    "Rest the pressure cooker off the heat for 30 minutes before opening, then discard the potli before blending.",
    "Add the milk gradually and keep the gravy at a gentle simmer; a hard boil can split the sauce.",
    "The 100 g butter goes into the gravy. The extra teaspoon is only for the coal bowl. The written method also adds butter to the tadka without giving a quantity; this card uses the 2 tbsp oil there instead."
